# Generated knowledge-graph output — regenerate with the graphify skill rather
# than tracking it; graph.json/graph.html alone are ~1.1 MB of derived data.
graphify-out/

# Claude Code machine-local settings (permissions etc.) — never commit
.claude/settings.local.json

# Environment files anywhere in the tree, including the repo ROOT.
#
# platform/.gitignore already covers the ones under platform/, but it cannot
# cover a `.env` dropped at the top level — and that is exactly where a guide,
# a tutorial or an AI assistant tells you to put one ("create a .env file in
# your project root"). THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. An untracked-but-not-ignored .env
# is one `git add -A` away from publishing a live gateway secret, which is the
# same trap the service-account rule below exists to close; google-services.json
# reached a commit that way on 2026-09-16.
#
# The negations keep the committed templates, which hold names and no values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

# Google service-account key files. They land in the repo root because that is
# where a browser download gets dragged, and they are untracked-but-not-ignored
# by default, which means `git add -A` commits a live private key. The name is
# always <project-id>-<key-id>.json.
*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f].json
gcp-*.json
service-account*.json

# Competitor APK and its decompile scratch directory (~200 MB). Kept on disk as
# a reference while the dialer work is live, but they are someone else's binary
# and a tool's output — neither belongs in this repo's history.
/ODialer.apk
/scratch_odialer/

# JVM crash dumps from Gradle/Android builds. They land next to the app module,
# are hundreds of KB of heap state, and say nothing about the source.
CallRecorderApp/hs_err_pid*.log

# Loose screenshots dragged to the repo root during UI work. Keep them on disk
# while a redesign is live; they are not source and the repo is public.
/*@1x.png
/*@2x.png

# Unreferenced scratch images in Build docs (~8 MB each). The docs themselves
# never link them, so they are someone's working material, not documentation.
Build docs/fairytale.png
Build docs/motu patlu.png
Build docs/superhero.png
